Greetings, Hard Chip players!

I've got a fresh update for you, and this one is a bit special (and continental). Hard Chip is starting to learn new languages – oui, oui, you read that right! We're dipping our toes into localization, with French leading the charge (and more languages on the horizon). On top of that, I've continued our never-ending war on "cheese" (those sneaky unintended solutions you clever folks come up with) and added a few nice quality-of-life improvements – including a darker, moodier look for the editor. Now, let's dive in and break down what's new and improved from version 0.0.6.78 to 0.0.6.80!



[h2]1. NEW French localization[/h2]
This is the big piece. The [b]French language is selectable from Settings[/b]! This update marks my first big push towards multi-language support. Making HC heavily hard-coded for English to handle those languages gracefully: French, German, Spanish, Russian, and Simplified Chinese are currently planned.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44903018/53dd652c0fdd5e185bd669cbff7f984774c71534.png[/img]

Obviously, the first localization run was to be my natural language: French! But everything is in place to handle other languages as well.

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/44903018/cbba91049a8ae9316108187c088d516f1955be32.png[/img]

As this is still a big piece, many bugs and translation errors might have found their way into the current version. Do not hesitate to join our Discord server and to use Steam Discussions to report any weird things!

